{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use small deterministic specifications to bind sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe recovery or exploration action. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, reserves move_backward only for front-obstacle escape, and uses full_rotate only from a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one-shot action states so each non-perception state enables exactly one controllable action",
    "Bias clear/path_clear outcomes to immediate forward progress",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Use move_backward only in dedicated front recovery",
    "Escalate to full_rotate only after repeated front-blocked recovery failure via a stuck helper state"
  ],
